.\" Cesar Log Viewer — Man Page
.TH CSL 1 "2026-08-02" "csl 0.0.7" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
csl \- Cesar service log viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B csl
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B csl
reads and renders the unified Markdown logs produced by the Cesar init system.
By default it shows the tail of all service logs; filters narrow it to a single
service, error level, or pattern. Without a matching service the program
reports that no logs were found.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-service \fINAME\fR
Restrict output to one service.
.TP
.B \-e, \-\-errors-only
Show only error-level entries.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-follow
Tail the logs and keep reading as new entries arrive.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-lines \fIN\fR
Number of lines to show (default 50).
.TP
.B \-g, \-\-grep \fIPATTERN\fR
Filter entries matching the pattern.
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-tree
Render entries as a tree grouped by service.
.TP
.B \-T, \-\-tail
Show only the tail of each service's log.
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-clear
Clear the log store.
.TP
.B \-S, \-\-stats
Show per-service statistics instead of raw entries.
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-summary
Print a summary of the log store.
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR csr (1)
